{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he shall offer it, etc., and make atonement, etc.</b> Meaning: corresponding to the offering of the lamb for a burnt-offering He said ״וְהִקְרִיבוֹ״, and corresponding to the young pigeon for a sin-offering He said <b>וְכִפֶּר עָלֶיהָ</b> — this is its plain sense. And in Torat Kohanim they expounded that the two do not hold each other back but only one; therefore He said ״וְהִקְרִיבוֹ״. And I do not know which of the two it is; when He says ״וְכִפֶּר״ etc. — atonement is through the sin-offering. Until here. Or perhaps they made the fine point from the fact that He did not say ״וְהִקְרִיבָם״, in which case He would not have needed to say ״וְכִפֶּר״ concerning the sin-offering. And even though He needed to say ״וְכִפֶּר״ according to the order stated concerning all the offerings, in any event He does not add a single word or a single letter if He says ״וְהִקְרִיבָם״ and registers the offering of them both."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:43.525833950Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}